                <pb facs="0498" n="380" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg380"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00Sonora/491: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Nogales</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Damm</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nogales, Ariz</hi></placeName>., <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-02T23:00:00-06:00">April 2, 1929—11
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 3—1:41 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Department’s April 2, 6 p.m. This Consulate has no information at present time
                    regarding wounding of Terry [<hi rendition="#italic">Harry</hi>] Baker at Naco,
                    Arizona, further than that contained in press dispatch which probably gave
                    accurate account.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Damm</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
